posts.body:
If you are talking about the substitute effect, I know that by default it is only triggered when an ally returns true to the "isDying()" method (and the hit is not "certain hit").
The "isDying()" threshold is 25% by default. Maybe something is changing it somewhere?
Code:
BattleManager.checkSubstitute = function(target) {
    return target.isDying() && !this._action.isCertainHit();
};

[...]

Game_BattlerBase.prototype.isDying = function() {
    return this.isAlive() && this._hp < this.mhp / 4;
};
